From: h713 <build@h713>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 18:30:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: h713: DEBUG cap the eMMC to 25 MHz

Debug only -- never put this in the shipping series.

The eMMC's read throughput is limited by its NAND at about 118 MB/s, far below
either candidate bus rate (400 MB/s if the card clock really is the labelled
200 MHz, 800 MB/s if it is the 400 MHz the CCU divider chain actually emits).
So a payload-timing probe at the normal rate measures the media and says
nothing about the clock.

Capping the ceiling to 25 MHz moves the bottleneck onto the bus, where the two
hypotheses separate cleanly:

  card clock == label   ->  25 MHz
  card clock == 2x label ->  50 MHz

Both are far under the 118 MB/s media ceiling, so whichever the probe measures
is the answer.  Drop the HS200/HS400/DDR mode flags too, so the card negotiates
a plain high-speed mode at that rate rather than failing to tune.

---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi | 5 +----
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 4 deletions(-)

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
@@ -901,10 +901,7 @@
 			bus-width = <8>;
 			non-removable;
 			cap-mmc-highspeed;
-			mmc-ddr-1_8v;
-			mmc-hs200-1_8v;
-			mmc-hs400-1_8v;
-			max-frequency = <200000000>;
+			max-frequency = <25000000>;
 			status = "okay";
 		};

